   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Getting_to_the_Point_%28album%29",
   "resumo_en": "Getting to the Point is the second studio album by English blues rock band Savoy Brown. It marks the debut of a vastly different lineup, still led by Kim Simmonds but fronted by new vocalist Chris Youlden.\nIt was released by Decca in 1968 with catalog number SKL 4935 and finds the group taking on more of the songwriting load, as opposed to their debut, which consisted mostly of covers. One of the covers is \"You Need Love\" by Willie Dixon, which served as a blueprint for \"Whole Lotta Love\" by Led Zeppelin. Deram released the cd with three bonus tracks in 1990 with catalog number 820 922–2.",
